`tools/decode-oracle/` is NOT covered by the Apache License above.

It is a separate Go module licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later, because it embeds QEMU's
decodetree tables. It is a developer-only analysis tool: it is never built into,
linked with, or shipped alongside the raptormark pipeline, and `go build ./...`
in this module does not descend into it -- there is no `go.work`, and nothing
in the root module imports it. Keeping it separate is what leaves this project
free to be Apache-2.0. See `tools/decode-oracle/README.md`.


Output of the pipeline carries licences this file says nothing about.

A module produced by raptormark contains code translated from whatever
container image was supplied as input, together with the ecvisor runtime. The
translated guest contents keep their own licences -- commonly glibc or musl,
among others -- and those terms are unaffected by this NOTICE. Anyone
distributing a translated module is responsible for the licences of the guest
image it was built from.
